Subject: [PATCH 07264/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5724: ThinkingCap-27B
 token-efficient reasoning test -- INCONCLUSIVE (raw-completion /think
 degenerate; needs chat-template retest)

Tests whether a model RL-tuned for ~50%-fewer-thinking-tokens (bottlecapai/
ThinkingCap-Qwen3.6-27B, Q4_K_M) completes genuine /think world-model induction
within the SAME 8192-token budget that vanilla Qwen3.5-9B-MTP overran on 0/N
(REQ-ARC-WMTE-5714's B2 finding). Faithful to that finding: induces via exp5714's
`_induce_no_fence` (codeonly OFF, /think, 8192, tries=1, NO pre-opened fence) --
NOT run_seeded_progress's built-in reason arm, whose real induce() fence-opener
suppresses the <think> trace -- composed with the REQ-ARC-WMTE-5720 downstream
ladder. Same 6-game roster (ls20 tr87 lp85 g50t m0r0 ft09) x2 trials, GPU 1,
queued behind and after the 5722/5723 run. Preflight verified real GPU offload
(VRAM 4->17176 MiB on load) + a /think /completion smoke round-trip.

Result: INCONCLUSIVE for the token-efficiency claim, and the reason is itself the
finding. On 10/12 ThinkingCap reason cells the model emitted an IMMEDIATE
end-of-sequence with ~0 output (stop_type=='eos', max_raw_completion_len~0, no
<think> trace) -- it generated essentially nothing, so those cells did NOT
genuinely test the budget hypothesis. This is a prompt-format artifact of the
no-fence RAW-/completion /think path, not a budget-overrun result. The SECONDARY
thinkingcap27_frozen codeonly arm induced cleanly on 12/12 cells (model/server/GPU
offload/plumbing all healthy), isolating the failure to the raw-completion
genuine-reasoning path -- ThinkingCap (Qwen3.6 base) likely needs its proper chat
template, which the raw /completion endpoint does not apply and which the older
Qwen3.5-9B baseline tolerates. Only the 2 genuine ThinkingCap attempts are
informative: 0/2 completed (1 overran the 8192 budget, 1 finished reasoning but
emitted unparseable code). The fresh Qwen3.5-9B-MTP reason baseline completed 1/12
(12/12 genuine attempts, 12 overran), reproducing the ~0/N budget wall of
REQ-ARC-WMTE-5714/5720.

Recommendation: re-test ThinkingCap through its proper Qwen3.6 chat template
(/chat/completions or an explicitly-templated assistant turn) before drawing any
budget-wall conclusion. Does NOT flip the frozen live default (operator-only).
adversarial_verify clean (0 flags); measurement_validity block + honest verdict
guard against a false "budget wall persists" negative.

